Hashmap involves storing key value pair.

In hashmap, entries are stored in ordered manner.

In hashing, operations like searching, inserting and deletion all occurs in O(1), whereas in array it will be
O(n).

Hashmap implements the Map Interface in the Collection Framework.

Hashmap uses hashtable for storage internally.

In hashmap value can be same but the key is unique.

The put method is used for both Insertion and Updation, if the key is present it will update otherwise it will
insert that key value pair.

The remove method is used for both deletion, if the key is present it will remove and return it otherwise it
will return null.

Sometimes, Hash Functions can result in same hash value for different keys. This is called Collisions.